                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Merv Reborn[/b] is a cheap looking platformer with poor controls and game mechanics. Had I not been asked to review this game, I would have never played it on my own accord.\n \n[h1][u]Positive:[/u][/h1]\n[list]\n[*]Music is decent. Arguably this best element of of Merv Reborn. \n[*]Fairly challenging. Difficulty progression is also decent as levels gradually get harder. Granted, some segments feel unfair because of the poor game mechanics, but overall it is quite manageable. \n[*]In Merv Reborn you are required to collect everything before heading to the goal. If you don’t collect everything, you are forced to restart the level. I liked that collectables were scattered around the map, which essentially forces you to explore every level thoroughly. It’s also nice that every level has a completely different layout and theme.\n[/list]\n \n[h1][u]Negative:[/u][/h1]\n[list]\n[*]I hate to say this, but this game looks awful. There is nothing alluring about the graphics.\n[*]Merv is very slow and the jump animation feels floaty. I especially disliked that pushing rocks was extremely slow. Playing Merv Reborn felt more like a chore than an enjoyable experience.\n[*]The game is described as a puzzle platformer but the only puzzle element is pushing rocks. It can also be frustrating that the rocks reset to their original position every time you die. \n[*]Double jump only works if you double jump directly after jumping. You cannot jump, pause and then double jump. This feels counterintuitive, and makes platforming awkward and unnecessarily difficult.\n[*]Merv can only move horizontally, so moving down a slope causes him to hop. If you pair that with Merv’s inability to double jump after a pause, it makes jumping off a slope unnecessarily difficult. This is especially frustrating because some segments require precision jumping off slopes.  \n[*]The last collectible in the last level requires obnoxious precision. There is very little room for error and no way around it because you are required to collect everything to finish a level.\n [/list]\n \n[h1][u]Conclusion:[/u][/h1]\n[h1]★✬☆☆☆ Mediocre[/h1]\n\nFrom the moment I first laid my eyes on Merv Reborn, I cringed. Just the trailer alone speaks volumes about the quality of this game. I really disliked the slow speed, the strange double jump mechanic, and the awkward movement on slopes. Playing Merv Reborn was not a pleasant experience for me and I found myself sighing with relief upon finishing it. There are higher quality games on Steam for free.\n\n[table]\n[tr]\n[th][h1]If you enjoyed this review please follow me on my [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/26827738-%27b-Reviews/?appid=241930]curator page[/url] and [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/breviews]group[/url]. Your time and support is greatly appreciated![/h1][/th]\n[/tr]\n[/table]",
